<title>JAPAN: Japan Sec to partly stop lending Tada Corp shares.</title>
<headline>Japan Sec to partly stop lending Tada Corp shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan Securities Finance Co Ltd (JSF) said on Tuesday that it would stop accepting orders to borrow shares of Tada Corp for certain margin transactions.</p>
<p>JSF said the move would be effective from Wednesday.</p>
<p>JSF is Japan's largest securities financing company and lends shares to brokerages for margin transactions with the authorisation of the Finance Ministry.</p>
<p>Shares of Tada Corp have been recently hurt by worries about the contractor's financial health.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, Tada Corp's shares ended 13 yen higher at 154.</p>
</text>
